      ]
     },
     "execution_count": 45,
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "execute_result"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# File-level: should be 1.0\n",
    "print(\"file overlap:\", len(eval_stems & set(anno_stems[anno_stems.isin(eval_stems)])) / len(eval_stems))\n",
    "\n",
    "# Label-level: should be close (small gap = raw-annotation-row vs extracted-clip granularity, not a bug)\n",
    "pd.DataFrame({\n",
    "    \"reconstructed\": holdout_eval_correct[\"Labels\"].value_counts(),\n",
    "    \"paper_truth\": birdnet01_DCLDE_eval[\"Truth\"].value_counts(),\n",
    "})"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "bc5d7b76",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# FINAL NOTE: We want to match on the file level in order to ensure that all is included is at the file level \n",
    "\n",
    "We are splitting at the file level and so in that case we are concerend with using every annotation for that given file.\n",
    "- before we were wrong because we were matching on incorrect indexes. \n",
    "- Now we need to split at the file level rather than the annotation level. "
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 46,
   "id": "3c76427a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
